    "body": "## Problem\n`vim.diagnostic.handlers.underline.show` throws `E565: Index out of bounds` when it tries to underline a diagnostic whose `lnum` is past the end of the buffer. This happens with stale diagnostics set on an unloaded buffer (e.g. via `bufadd()`) that are drawn only after the buffer is loaded: by then the file on disk can be shorter than the `lnum` the diagnostic carried. File pickers (snacks.nvim) that open files via `bufadd` + `:buffer` hit this whenever an LSP server has already emitted diagnostics for that URI.\n\n## Fix\nSkip diagnostics with an out-of-range `lnum` in the underline handler, mirroring the guard already present in the signs handler (#29321). The location-extmark setup in `vim.diagnostic.set` already clamps the same way, so this makes the three code paths consistent.\n\nCloses #40838\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-20T10:59:21Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "There are similar handlers in the same file, `M.virtual_text.show()`, `M.signs.show()`, maybe others. They have the same handling, so this LGTM. (In the future, please look for things like that and call them out in the PR, so reviewers don't have to.)\r\n\r\nMeanwhile, it sureeeeee seems like these handlers could share a common function so that we don't have to fix the same bugs for each of them... sigh.",
